course: dictionary
lesson: 9155
title: Snoring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Snoring is the loud, rough sound some people and animals make when they breathe while they are asleep. As a verb, snore means making that sound. «Grandpa was snoring away in his chair» means he was making that sound right then.
explain: Why does it happen? «Snoring is the noise of air rattling soft parts of the throat in sleep.» When air rushes past the soft parts at the back of the throat and nose, they shake, and the shaking makes the noise.
explain: Use the words around snoring to work out its meaning. In «loud snoring», the word loud tells you it is a noise you can hear clearly. In «stop snoring», stop tells you it is something that can be ended. A story might make snoring funny, like a giant snoring in a cave, but in health lessons it is about how the body works.
fact: Snoring means the loud, rough sound made while breathing in sleep.
fact: Snoring is a noun for the sound itself, and snore is the verb for making it.
fact: Snoring happens when air shakes the soft parts of the throat and nose.
fact: «Loud snoring» means a very noisy sound from someone asleep.
fact: A cold can make you snore, because a blocked nose changes how air moves.
exercise: «Snoring is the noise of air rattling soft parts of the throat in sleep.» What is snoring? | A loud sound made while running fast | *A rough sound made while breathing in sleep | A soft bed for sleeping on | A kind of food eaten before bed
exercise: Grandpa is «snoring away» in his chair. What is he doing right now? | Reading a book quietly | Eating his dinner | Singing a song loudly | *Making a rough breathing sound while asleep
exercise: «Loud snoring» keeps everyone awake. What does loud tell you about the snoring? | *It is a very loud sound | It is a kind of food | It is a happy game | It is a very quiet sound
test: What causes snoring, according to the lesson? | Eating sweets before bed | *Air shaking the soft parts of the throat and nose | Reading in bed | Too much sunshine during the day
test: What does «snoring away» mean? | *Snoring steadily while asleep | Talking in a loud whisper | Running away very quickly | Singing a song very softly
exam: Why might a cold make someone snore? | *Because a blocked nose changes how air moves through the throat | Because colds make people run faster | Because colds make hair grow longer | Because snoring is a kind of food
